role: r0-coverage
claim: For every N>=2, the uniform identity bridge at L_N=2N^3 misses some transposition with probability at most exp(-2N); for N>=3 the stronger all-even-L bound (2.1) holds.
status: proved
assumptions: The established Caputo--Liggett--Richthammer Theorem 1.1 on equality of interchange and one-particle spectral gaps; no conjectural project assumption.
evidence: Theorem 2.1 and its convention-complete proof above; exact_coverage_check.py; exact_check_results.json.
independent_checks: A separate P-versus-Q operator perturbation derivation, exact return/coverage DP through N=5, symbolic spectral constants through N=12; fresh-worker audit pending coordinator assignment.
complexity: The theorem is analytic and introduces no sampler state or coverage mask. For one alphabet the checker uses O(L N! binom(N,2)) time and O(N!) memory; checking every deleted edge adds another binom(N,2) time factor, and the support-mask DP is used only in tiny cases. It is validation, not the proposed sampler.
first_unproved_step: None for R0; only the run-mandated independent human/worker audit remains before coordinator acceptance.
verdict: promote
implementation specification.  No durable shared file was edited in this
worker run.

role: r1-bijection
claim: For every N>=2, L>=0, g in S_N, and every old/star binary pattern, the explicit stable-sort map is a product-preserving bijection with star endpoint h^{-1}g, and summing it proves (D).
status: proved
assumptions: Permutations are maps with (alpha beta)(x)=alpha(beta(x)); group-algebra zeroth powers equal the unit; the exact-uniform corollary assumes access to exact nonempty branch and fiber samplers.
evidence: Complete elementary proof above; check_disintegration.py; results.jsonl and summary.json give 1,064 all-endpoint coefficient checks and 1,168,198 exhaustive inverse-bijection cases through N=5,L=6 with zero failures.
independent_checks: Direct endpoint DP versus old/star convolution; leftmost versus rightmost rewriting; closed suffix formula; both inverse round trips; feasibility DP; fresh coordinator audit still required by the run protocol.
complexity: Forward and inverse word maps take O(k(L-k)) <= O(L^2) constant-time endpoint updates and O(L) storage; R1 alone does not solve the R2/R3 branch or star sampling complexity.
first_unproved_step: None inside R1; at sampler level, the first remaining step is a positive polynomial-time sampler for the weighted (k,h) branch together with prescribed-endpoint star fibers.
verdict: promote
use the dense sampler with an explicit telescope.  The present report proves
neither alternative.

role: r2-branch
claim: The positive two-sided labeled branch sampler (11) has d_TV at most Delta/(1-Delta) uniformly over feasible g whenever Delta<1, and at L=2N^3 this is at most 2 exp(-N^2/2); exact arbitrary-short R2 reduces to the stated positive stabilizer-connection sampler.
status: proved
assumptions: Exact fair random bits; the standard transposition character-ratio spectrum and Jucys--Murphy content spectrum audited above; the finalized R3 theorem when a conditional star word is requested in the star-long branch.
evidence: Sections 2--8 give the positive algorithm, pointwise proof, state and bit complexity, dense specialization, boundaries, and scoped type-table obstruction; branch_audit.py and results.json give all-endpoint exact checks.
independent_checks: The fresh R6 implementation independently reproduced the formulas and all exact dense maxima/bounds for every feasible endpoint at N=4,L=128 and N=5,L=250; its checkpoint.md and results.json report no mismatch.
complexity: O(L) polynomial-bit states and polynomial Turing time for the branch draw, with O(L^2 log N) conservative expected random bits; composing the star-long branch with R3 costs its conservative O(N^3 L^3) exact-rational operations and preserves TV.
first_unproved_step: Prove the positive stabilizer-connection sampler above, or prove an R4/R5 internal-length invariant and summable telescope that never requires it outside negligible mass.
verdict: promote
and sample the actual labeled `h` without enumerating `S_(N-1)`.  This report
does not claim that the full rank recursion is polynomial.

role: r3-star
claim: Every feasible prescribed-endpoint length-k star bridge in S_N can be counted and sampled exactly in expected time polynomial in N and k by positive exact-support decomposition, Féray's transitive coefficient formula, and labeled last-factor recursion.
status: proved
assumptions: Exact fair random bits for weighted draws; audited use of Féray Theorem 1.2 under the identical map-composition convention.
