Completed. Final classification: `strict-reduction`.

The run proved:

- A polynomial-time rank-recursive sampler with exact endpoint and
  \[
  d_{\mathrm{TV}}\le 3N e^{-N/12288}
  \]
  at \(L=2N^3\), with conservative complexity \(O(N^4L^3)\).
- Dense complete-support failure at most \(e^{-2N}\).
- The stable-sort disintegration and inverse bijection exactly.
- An exact polynomial-time prescribed-endpoint star-bridge sampler.
- A rigorous obstruction to the specified symmetrized paired-lift/Hurwitz architecture.

The classification is conservative because the sampler’s negligible error is fixed by \(N,L\); it cannot yet satisfy arbitrary requested \(\epsilon<3Ne^{-N/12288}\) in polynomial \(\log(1/\epsilon)\) time. The remaining standalone problem is the tunable positive connection lemma.

